50,3,1,talk,Rin,,Free Address sounds like a nightmare for my schedule. Rotating Blocks is too much packing. Fixed Desks seems safest.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Fixed Desks by Function avoids repeated facilities charges and keeps the budget stable. I vote for C.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Free Address is unfair due to arrival times. Rotating Blocks is chaotic. I'll go with Fixed Desks.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shion,,I can't do Free Address or Rotating Blocks; I need my physical settings to stay put. Fixed Desks it is.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I love the idea of Rotating Blocks for meeting new people, but Fixed Desks by Function keeps project partners together.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Rin,,I agree. Let's just pick the one that doesn't make us move every week.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Toshio,,It is the most logical choice for the budget.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,It allows us to explicitly decide who gets the window seats too.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shion,,"As long as I'm away from the printer, I'm happy.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I'll vote for Fixed Desks to ensure the project strands stay close.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm voting C!,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
